@startuml
title ParametricCAD — interactive Push/Pull

skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor User
participant CadViewer as Viewer
participant "V3d_View" as View
participant PushPullDrag as DragMath
participant MainWindow
participant ModelingController as Controller
participant QUndoStack as Stack
participant AddFeatureCommand as Command
participant PushPullFeature as Feature
participant ModelPresenter as Presenter

User -> Viewer : press P and click planar face
Viewer -> Viewer : capture face ID, face index, normal
Viewer -> View : ConvertWithProj(mouse position)
View --> Viewer : world ray
Viewer -> DragMath : create drag state(anchor, normal, camera)
DragMath --> Viewer : drag plane

loop mouse move
    User -> Viewer : move cursor
    Viewer -> View : ConvertWithProj(current position)
    View --> Viewer : world ray
    Viewer -> DragMath : intersect ray with drag plane
    DragMath --> Viewer : world point and distance
    Viewer -> Viewer : build preview from absolute distance
    Viewer -> Viewer : update temporary AIS preview
end

User -> Viewer : release / confirm
Viewer -> MainWindow : commit(targetId, faceIndex, normal, distance)
MainWindow -> Controller : pushPull(...)
Controller -> Feature : construct PushPullFeature
Controller -> Stack : push(AddFeatureCommand)
Stack -> Command : redo()
Command -> Feature : insert and recompute
Feature --> Command : fused or cut shape
Stack -> MainWindow : indexChanged()
MainWindow -> Presenter : refresh()
Presenter -> Viewer : replace preview with model presentation

note over DragMath
  Distance is projected in world space:
  ray -> drag plane -> delta · normal

  No pixels-to-model coefficient.
  A head-on normal uses a stable
  camera-up depth-control fallback.
end note

note over Viewer,Feature
  Preview is transient.
  Commit creates exactly one undoable
  model operation.
end note
@enduml
